--TEST--
A session read inside `Core\Html::later` and `Core\Task::afterResponse` compiles, because a read sends no header. Inside `later` it returns the value the main script saved; work after the response has no request, so its read throws `LogicError` -- `rule:core-classes/html-later`, `rule:concurrency/deferred-work-cannot-write-the-response`
--SKIPIF--
<?nvs
// The record crosses the store `[cache.shared]` names, and a tree without one
// skips. The store is checked directly, because the session throws where no
// request arrived.
try {
    Core\Cache::shared()->get("whether-a-session-case-has-a-store-to-cross");
} catch (Throwable $nowhere) {
    echo "skip - ", $nowhere->message, "\n";
}
--GET--
under=a-request
--FILE--
<?nvs
// The main script saves a value. A part of the page filled later reads it.
// Work after the response runs without the request, so its read throws.
Core\Session::setShortLived("cart", 3);
echo Core\Html::later(fn(): void => {
    echo "later reads ", Core\Session::get("cart") as int, "\n";
});
Core\Task::afterResponse(fn(): void => {
    try {
        var $cart = Core\Session::get("cart");
        echo "after the response reads ", $cart as int, "\n";
    } catch (LogicError $e) {
        echo "after the response, the read compiles and throws LogicError\n";
    }
});
--FILE nvs.toml--
# One shared store, as the other session cases use. `redis` is
# `tests/db/compose.yaml`'s service.
[capabilities.cache]
shared = true

[session]
backend = "shared"

[cache.shared]
url = "redis://127.0.0.1:16379"
--EXPECT--
later reads 3
after the response, the read compiles and throws LogicError
